        {
          "type": "terms",
          "items": [
            [
              "Index",
              "Position of a character; first is 0, last is −1."
            ],
            [
              "Slice",
              "s[start:end:step]; end is excluded."
            ],
            [
              "Immutable",
              "Can't be changed in place."
            ],
            [
              "Method",
              "A function attached to a value: s.upper()."
            ],
            [
              "in",
              "True if a substring occurs."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "warn",
          "md": "- **Off by one**: `s[1]` is the **second** character; `s[0:3]` has 3 characters (0, 1, 2).\n- **Index past the end**: `s[len(s)]` is an IndexError (slices never are).\n- **Expecting methods to change s**: `s.upper()` returns a new string; `s` is unchanged unless reassigned.",
          "title": "Classic mistakes"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "exam",
          "md": "Exam 1 was in class on Canvas with the Respondus LockDown Browser: multiple choice, about 40 minutes, no AI tools. Its review list: computational-thinking terms, indexing, data types, data structures, input/print, logical and arithmetic operators, strings, flowcharts and pseudocode, variables, sequence, selection, repetition, functions.",
          "title": "How Exam 1 tested this"
        }
